  <entry>
    <title>Convex Hull Trick</title>
    <link href="/2026/10/03/Convex%20Hull%20Trick/"/>
    <url>/2026/10/03/Convex%20Hull%20Trick/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="convex-hull-trick">Convex Hull Trick</h1><p>The Convex Hull Trick can speed up a dynamic programming transitionby treating each previous state as a line. In this post, we will derivethis transformation for a partitioning problem and explain how amonotonic deque reduces the running time from<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^2)</annotation></semantics></math>to<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p><h2 id="problem-analysis">Problem analysis</h2><h3 id="starting-with-a-quadratic-dp">Starting with a quadratic DP</h3><p>Consider <a href="https://loj.ac/p/10188">HNOI2008 ToyPacking</a>.</p><p>There are<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>items arranged in a line. The<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-thitem has length<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_i</annotation></semantics></math>,and we need to partition the items into contiguous groups. For a group<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[l,r]</annotation></semantics></math>,the cost is</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(r-l+\sum_{k=l}^{r}c_k-L\right)^2,</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>where<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>is a constant. The term<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r-l</annotation></semantics></math>accounts for the one-unit gap between each pair of adjacent items in thegroup. Our goal is to minimize the total cost of all groups.</p><p>The constraints are</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\le n\le 5\times 10^4,\qquad 1\le L,c_i\le 10^7.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Let<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i</annotation></semantics></math>denote the minimum total cost of partitioning the first<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>items. Define the prefix sums as</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_i=\sum_{k=1}^{i}c_k,\qquad S_0=f_0=0.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>If the final group contains items<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j+1</annotation></semantics></math>through<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,its total length is<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_i-S_j+i-j-1</annotation></semantics></math>.Considering every possible starting position of this final group givesthe recurrence</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned}f_i&amp;=\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{f_j+\left(i-(j+1)+S_i-S_j-L\right)^2\right\}\\&amp;=\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{f_j+\left(S_i-S_j+i-j-1-L\right)^2\right\}.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>This straightforward solution checks every previous state for each<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,resulting in an<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^2)</annotation></semantics></math>algorithm.</p><h3 id="rewriting-the-transition">Rewriting the transition</h3><p>Expanding the square allows us to separate the terms that depend onlyon<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>from those involving<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p><p>Let<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_i=S_i+i</annotation></semantics></math>.We can then write</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_i-S_j+i-j-1-L=a_i-a_j-L-1.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Now let<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_i=a_i-L-1</annotation></semantics></math>.The recurrence becomes</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned}f_i&amp;=\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{f_j+(x_i-a_j)^2\right\}\\&amp;=x_i^2+\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{-2a_jx_i+f_j+a_j^2\right\}.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>For a fixed<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,the term<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_i^2</annotation></semantics></math>is the same for every candidate<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>,so it can be moved outside the minimum.</p><h3 id="interpreting-each-state-as-a-line">Interpreting each state as aline</h3><p>For each previous state<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>,define a line</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_j(x)=k_jx+b_j,</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>where</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_j=-2a_j=-2(S_j+j),\qquadb_j=f_j+a_j^2=f_j+(S_j+j)^2.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Computing<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i</annotation></semantics></math>now requires finding the minimum value among these lines at<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x_i</annotation></semantics></math>,then adding<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_i^2</annotation></semantics></math>:</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i=x_i^2+\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\ell_j(x_i).</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Once we have computed<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i</annotation></semantics></math>,we can construct its line and make it available to subsequent states. Wequery before inserting the new line because only states with<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;i</annotation></semantics></math>are valid candidates.</p><h2 id="maintaining-the-candidate-lines">Maintaining the candidatelines</h2><p>To speed up the transition, we discard lines that cannot improve theanswer to any future query. However, we cannot keep only the line thatis currently optimal: a different line may become optimal as the querycoordinate changes.</p><p>We will use a deque under two conditions:</p><ul><li>Lines are inserted in strictly decreasing order of slope.</li><li>Query coordinates are nondecreasing.</li></ul><p>The first condition lets us remove redundant lines from the back ofthe deque. The second lets us discard lines from the front as we answerqueries.</p><h3 id="adding-a-new-line">Adding a new line</h3><p>Consider three lines<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>,<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>,and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>with strictly decreasing slopes:</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_P&gt;k_Q&gt;k_R.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>The<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinateof the intersection of<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>is</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(P,Q)=\frac{b_Q-b_P}{k_P-k_Q}.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>For<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>to be no higher than both<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>,we need</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(P,Q)\le x\le X(Q,R).</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Therefore, if</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(P,Q)\ge X(Q,R),</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>then<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>is never strictly better than both<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.When the two intersection coordinates are equal, all three lines meet atthe same point, so<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>can still be removed without changing the minimum value.</p><p>When inserting a new line<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>,we apply this test to the last two lines in the deque and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.If the middle line is redundant, we remove it from the back and repeatthe test. We then append<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p><h3 id="answering-queries">Answering queries</h3><p>Suppose the first two lines in the deque are<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>and<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>,with<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_P&gt;k_Q</annotation></semantics></math>.If, at the current query coordinate<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>,</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)\le P(x),</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>then<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>remains no higher than<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>for every later coordinate. To see why, let<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&#39;\ge x</annotation></semantics></math>.We have</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x&#39;)-P(x&#39;)=Q(x)-P(x)+(k_Q-k_P)(x&#39;-x)\le 0.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>We can therefore remove<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>from the front of the deque. We repeat this comparison until only oneline remains or the first line is better than the second at the currentcoordinate.</p><p>The insertion step keeps the intersection coordinates of consecutivelines in increasing order. This ensures that, once the front comparisonsstop, the first line gives the minimum value among all remainingcandidates.</p><h2 id="applying-the-optimization">Applying the optimization</h2><p>Returning to our problem, we have</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i+1}-a_i=c_{i+1}+1&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Thus,<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>is strictly increasing. The inserted slopes<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_j=-2a_j</annotation></semantics></math>are strictly decreasing, and the query coordinates<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_i=a_i-L-1</annotation></semantics></math>are strictly increasing. Both conditions required by the deque aresatisfied.</p><p>Each line is inserted once and removed at most once, from either end.Although a single operation may remove several lines, there are only<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>removals over the entire algorithm. The total running time is therefore<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>,with<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>space in the worst case.</p><h2 id="understanding-the-implementation">Understanding theimplementation</h2><h3 id="matching-the-code-to-the-recurrence">Matching the code to therecurrence</h3><p>The implementation below uses an equivalent arrangement of the samerecurrence. It keeps the query coordinate at<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>and includes the constant<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L+1</annotation></semantics></math>in each line instead.</p><p>Define</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_j=a_j+L+1.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Then</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right" style="text-align: right; padding-right: 0"></mtd><mtd columnalign="left" style="text-align: left; padding-left: 0"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><munder><mi mathvariant="normal">min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="true" form="prefix">{</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="true" form="postfix">}</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned}f_i&amp;=\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{f_j+(a_i-t_j)^2\right\}\\&amp;=a_i^2+\min_{0\le j&lt;i}\left\{(-2t_j)a_i+f_j+t_j^2\right\}.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>The code therefore uses the following quantities:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>s[i]</code></td><td>The prefix sum<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>f[i]</code></td><td>The minimum cost<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>x = s[i] + i</code></td><td>The current query coordinate<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>t</code></td><td>The value<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_j=a_j+L+1</annotation></semantics></math>for the state whose line is being constructed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>line.fir</code></td><td>The slope<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2t_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>line.sec</code></td><td>The intercept<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_j+t_j^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Here, <code>fir</code> and <code>sec</code> are macros for<code>first</code> and <code>second</code>. The deque stores each lineas a pair containing its slope and intercept. Since adding<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L+1</annotation></semantics></math>preserves the order of the<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_j</annotation></semantics></math>values, the slopes still decrease and the query coordinates stillincrease.</p><h3 id="initializing-the-deque">Initializing the deque</h3><p>The initial candidate is state<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math>,where<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_0=f_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>.Therefore,<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_0=L+1</annotation></semantics></math>,and its line is</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=-2(L+1)x+(L+1)^2.</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>This explains the initialization <code>t = L + 1</code> and<code>q.push_back({-2 * t, t * t})</code>. State<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>represents placing all of the first<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>items into a single group. The global arrays are zero-initialized,providing <code>s[0] = f[0] = 0</code>.</p><h3 id="querying-the-minimum">Querying the minimum</h3><p>The helper <code>value(line, x)</code> evaluates a line at thecurrent coordinate. In the first <code>while</code> loop, if<code>q[1]</code> is no higher than <code>q[0]</code>, the first linecan be removed permanently. The <code>&lt;=</code> comparison alsohandles ties: the second line has a smaller slope and is at least asgood for every future query.</p><p>After this loop, <code>q.front()</code> gives the minimum line value,so the assignment <code>f[i] = x*x + value(q.front(), x)</code> computesthe current DP state.</p><h3 id="inserting-the-current-state">Inserting the current state</h3><p>After computing <code>f[i]</code>, the code sets<code>t = x + L + 1</code>. Since <code>x = a_i</code>, this is exactly<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_i=a_i+L+1</annotation></semantics></math>.The new line <code>R</code> has slope<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2t_i</annotation></semantics></math>and intercept<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_i+t_i^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p><p>The helper <code>check(A, B, C)</code> determines whether the middleline <code>B</code> is redundant. It tests</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(A,B)\ge X(B,C).</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>Because<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_A&gt;k_B&gt;k_C</annotation></semantics></math>,both denominators in the intersection formulas are positive. We cantherefore compare the intersections by cross multiplication:</p><p><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_B-b_A)(k_B-k_C)\ge(k_A-k_B)(b_C-b_B).</annotation></semantics></math></p><p>This is the expression used in <code>check</code>, avoiding divisionwhen comparing intersection coordinates. The second <code>while</code>loop removes redundant lines from the back, and<code>q.push_back(R)</code> makes the new state available to futurequeries.</p><h2 id="code">Code</h2><figure class="highlight c++"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br><span class="line">16</span><br><span class="line">17</span><br><span class="line">18</span><br><span class="line">19</span><br><span class="line">20</span><br><span class="line">21</span><br><span class="line">22</span><br><span class="line">23</span><br><span class="line">24</span><br><span class="line">25</span><br><span class="line">26</span><br><span class="line">27</span><br><span class="line">28</span><br><span class="line">29</span><br><span class="line">30</span><br><span class="line">31</span><br><span class="line">32</span><br><span class="line">33</span><br><span class="line">34</span><br><span class="line">35</span><br><span class="line">36</span><br><span class="line">37</span><br><span class="line">38</span><br><span class="line">39</span><br><span class="line">40</span><br><span class="line">41</span><br><span class="line">42</span><br><span class="line">43</span><br><span class="line">44</span><br><span class="line">45</span><br><span class="line">46</span><br><span class="line">47</span><br><span class="line">48</span><br><span class="line">49</span><br><span class="line">50</span><br><span class="line">51</span><br><span class="line">52</span><br><span class="line">53</span><br><span class="line">54</span><br><span class="line">55</span><br><span class="line">56</span><br><span class="line">57</span><br><span class="line">58</span><br><span class="line">59</span><br><span class="line">60</span><br><span class="line">61</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs c++"><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">include</span><span class="hljs-string">&lt;iostream&gt;</span></span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">include</span><span class="hljs-string">&lt;utility&gt;</span></span><br><br><span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">namespace</span> std;<br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> ll long long</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> ls(x) (x &lt;&lt; 1)</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> rs(x) (x &lt;&lt; 1 | 1)</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> mp make_pair</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> fir first</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> sec second</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> pi pair<span class="hljs-string">&lt;int,int&gt;</span></span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> sec second</span><br><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> pi pair<span class="hljs-string">&lt;int,int&gt;</span></span><br><br><span class="hljs-type">const</span> <span class="hljs-type">int</span> maxn = <span class="hljs-number">5</span> * <span class="hljs-number">1e4</span> + <span class="hljs-number">514</span>;<br>ll n, L;<br>ll c[maxn];<br>ll f[maxn], s[maxn];<br><br><span class="hljs-function">ll <span class="hljs-title">value</span><span class="hljs-params">(<span class="hljs-type">const</span> pair&lt;ll,ll&gt;&amp; line, ll x)</span></span>&#123;<br><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> line.fir * x + line.sec;<br>&#125;<br><br><span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-keyword">inline</span> <span class="hljs-type">bool</span> <span class="hljs-title">check</span><span class="hljs-params">(pair&lt;ll,ll&gt; A, pair&lt;ll,ll&gt; B, pair&lt;ll,ll&gt; C)</span></span>&#123;<br><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> (B.sec - A.sec) * (B.fir - C.fir) &gt;= (A.fir - B.fir) * (C.sec - B.sec);<br>&#125;<br><br><span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-type">int</span> <span class="hljs-title">main</span><span class="hljs-params">()</span></span>&#123;<br>std::ios::<span class="hljs-built_in">sync_with_stdio</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">false</span>);<br>std::cin.<span class="hljs-built_in">tie</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">nullptr</span>); std::cout.<span class="hljs-built_in">tie</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">nullptr</span>);<br><br>std::cin &gt;&gt; n &gt;&gt; L;<br><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span>(<span class="hljs-type">int</span> i = <span class="hljs-number">1</span>; i &lt;= n; ++i)&#123;<br>std::cin &gt;&gt; c[i];<br>s[i] = c[i] + s[i - <span class="hljs-number">1</span>];<br>&#125;<br>ll t = L + <span class="hljs-number">1</span>;<br>deque&lt; pair&lt;ll, ll&gt; &gt; q; <span class="hljs-comment">// K &amp; B</span><br>q.<span class="hljs-built_in">push_back</span>(&#123;<span class="hljs-number">-2</span> * t, t * t&#125;);<br><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span>(<span class="hljs-type">int</span> i = <span class="hljs-number">1</span>; i &lt;= n; ++i)&#123;<br>ll x = s[i] + i;<br>pair&lt;ll,ll&gt; tmp;<br><br><span class="hljs-keyword">while</span>(q.<span class="hljs-built_in">size</span>() &gt;= <span class="hljs-number">2</span> &amp;&amp; <span class="hljs-built_in">value</span>(q[<span class="hljs-number">1</span>], x) &lt;= <span class="hljs-built_in">value</span>(q[<span class="hljs-number">0</span>], x))&#123;<br>q.<span class="hljs-built_in">pop_front</span>();<br>&#125;<br><br>f[i] = x*x + <span class="hljs-built_in">value</span>(q.<span class="hljs-built_in">front</span>(), x);<br>t = x + L + <span class="hljs-number">1</span>;<br><span class="hljs-keyword">auto</span> R = <span class="hljs-built_in">mp</span>(<span class="hljs-number">-2</span> * t, f[i] + t * t);<br><br><span class="hljs-keyword">while</span>(q.<span class="hljs-built_in">size</span>() &gt;= <span class="hljs-number">2</span> &amp;&amp; <span class="hljs-built_in">check</span>(q[q.<span class="hljs-built_in">size</span>() - <span class="hljs-number">2</span>], q.<span class="hljs-built_in">back</span>(), R))&#123;<br>q.<span class="hljs-built_in">pop_back</span>();<br>&#125;<br><br>q.<span class="hljs-built_in">push_back</span>(R);<br>&#125;<br>std::cout &lt;&lt; f[n] &lt;&lt; endl;<br><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span>;<br>&#125;<br><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure>]]></content>
    
    
